<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  HYBRID GALLERY — the mark.

  ## What the shape means

  An H, because that is the product's initial, built from two overlapping frames
  rather than from strokes. Two frames that share a spine is what "hybrid" means here:
  two libraries, one view. The overlap is filled solid, so the joint reads as a single
  bright element instead of a seam.

  ## Why it is drawn this way

  The mark contains no circle, no burst and no flower. Those are the stock gallery
  silhouettes, and the previous six-petal artwork read as a Huawei imitation in review.
  A square-with-a-cross is also out: it is the "broken image" glyph, and a gallery that
  shows it as its own logo is telling the wrong story.

  ## Construction

  A 108 x 108 viewport with the artwork inside the 72 x 72 safe circle, which is what
  the adaptive-icon spec asks for: 18 dp of bleed on every side at mdpi.
  - Left frame: x 22..52, y 30..78, corner radius 5.
  - Right frame: x 56..86, y 30..78, corner radius 5.
  - Spine: x 49..59, y 30..78 — the two frames overlap it, which produces the H.
  - A single dot sits in the left frame: the "one photo" that any library starts with.

  Every coordinate is a whole number on a 4-unit grid, so the mark stays crisp at 24 dp.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- Left frame: the gallery that was already there. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M27,30 L47,30 A5,5 0 0 1 52,35 L52,73 A5,5 0 0 1 47,78 L27,78 A5,5 0 0 1 22,73 L22,35 A5,5 0 0 1 27,30 Z"
        android:fillColor="#5AA6FF"
        android:fillAlpha="0.92" />

    <!-- Right frame: the second source. Offset by four units so the two never merge. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M61,30 L81,30 A5,5 0 0 1 86,35 L86,73 A5,5 0 0 1 81,78 L61,78 A5,5 0 0 1 56,73 L56,35 A5,5 0 0 1 61,30 Z"
        android:fillColor="#FF8A63"
        android:fillAlpha="0.92" />

    <!-- The spine: drawn last so it sits on top and joins the two frames into an H. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M49,30 L59,30 L59,78 L49,78 Z"
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF" />

    <!-- One photograph, already in the library. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M32,58 m-4,0 a4,4 0 1,0 8,0 a4,4 0 1,0 -8,0"
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:fillAlpha="0.95" />
</vector>
